    <!-- About Screen -->
    <string name="about_subtitle">Learn more about Sentry Rack</string>
    <string name="about_description">Sentry Rack is a rack-level monitoring platform that turns raw sensor data (security, current, environment and leak detection) into clear insights about server rack health.</string>
    <string name="about_monitor_header">What we monitor</string>
    <string name="about_monitor_door">Rack door security</string>
    <string name="about_monitor_power">Power usage</string>
    <string name="about_monitor_environment">Temperature and air quality</string>
    <string name="about_monitor_leak">Water leaks</string>
    <string name="about_team_header">Our team</string>
    <string name="about_member_1" translatable="false">Andres \"Jack of all trades, master of none\" Zambrano</string>
    <string name="about_member_2" translatable="false">Duc Anh \"The Hater\" Volk</string>
    <string name="about_member_3" translatable="false">Anvesh \"The crafty pretender\" Rachakonda</string>
    <string name="about_member_4" translatable="false">Krushna \"The privileged sweet talker\" Patel</string>
    <string name="about_group" translatable="false">Group KAVA · Humber Polytechnic</string>
    <string name="about_copyright">© 2026 Sentry Rack. All rights reserved.</string>
    <string name="about_message"><![CDATA[Let\'s just call it how it is. If you claim to have a passion for some kind of art or hobby and you use artificial intelligence for any step of that process, you should just give up. The reality is AI has never been and will never be just a tool. It is a fast-forward button for lazy or talentless people to skip past the difficult part of a project. And I think that is where so many people misinterpret what art really is. 10% of the effort that goes on behind a film or a book or a painting was finding the idea. The rest was the journey. The rest was the struggles that went behind actually carrying it out. That is what makes something beautiful. And if you\'re using a program to promt your way to the finish line, at the end of the day, you\'re not an artist. You\'re someone who knows how to work a keyboard.]]></string>

